│ Okay, let's address this issue. The core problem is that Sphinx    │
│ isn't documenting methods decorated with both @classmethod and     │
│ @property due to how type() is used to determine the docstring     │
│ source. The fix, as suggested in the issue and confirmed by the    │
│ bug report, is to use __doc__ directly instead of relying on       │
│ type() to infer the docstring source.  This change is already      │
│ implemented in Python 3.10 and later. Since we are working with a  │
│ 3.9 environment, we need to manually add the __doc__ attribute to  │
│ the class property.                                                │
