│ Okay, let's address this issue. The core problem is that Sphinx    │
│ isn't documenting methods decorated with both @classmethod and     │
│ @property due to how type() is used to determine the               │
│ documentation. The bug report highlights that                      │
│ type(BaseClass.baseclass_property) returns property, which doesn't │
│ trigger Sphinx's documentation extraction, while                   │
│ type(BaseClass.baseclass_class_property) returns the type of the   │
│ returned object.                                                   │
│                                                                    │
│ The fix involves modifying the code to explicitly use __doc__ to   │
│ access the documentation string, regardless of whether the         │
│ decorated element is a property or a class method. This will force │
│ Sphinx to correctly extract the documentation for these methods.   │
│                                                                    │
│ Here's the patch:                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
