│ Okay, let's address this issue. The core problem is that Sphinx    │
│ isn't documenting methods decorated with both @classmethod and     │
│ @property due to how type() is used to determine the docstring     │
│ source. The bug report highlights that                             │
│ type(BaseClass.baseclass_property) returns property, which doesn't │
│ trigger docstring extraction, while                                │
│ type(BaseClass.baseclass_class_property) returns the type of the   │
│ returned object.                                                   │
│                                                                    │
│ The proposed fix, as suggested in the bug report and confirmed by  │
│ Python 3.10, is to leverage the __doc__ attribute directly on the  │
│ class method and property, rather than relying on type() to        │
│ determine the docstring source. This is now the standard behavior  │
│ in Python 3.10.                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│ Here’s the patch:                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
